#: processes/sdlc/test-data-curation.bpmn:18
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "General curation process for fixed (`test-data-fixed/1.0.0`) and generated (`test-data-generated/1.0.0`) test data sets — bean `folio-assistant-vm6m`, companion `folio-assistant-vljz`, proposal `docs/proposals/qa-reports-branch-and-test-process-2026-10-01.md` §3.2. SEPARATE GRAPH DIRECTORIES, SELF-IDENTIFYING FILES. Fixed sets live in a declared `test-data-fixed` directory and generated recipes live in a declared `test-data-generated` directory (`schemas/graph-typology-registry.ts`). Every file carries both its `$schema` tag (`test-data-fixed/1.0.0` vs `test-data-generated/1.0.0`) and `kind: \"fixed\" | \"generated\"` (`schemas/test-data.ts`), so a consumer (`discriminateTestDataSet`) tells which it is reading from the file content, never from the directory path. CONTENT-TYPE SPECIALISATION AS A CALLED SUBPROCESS. How a recipe synthesises test inputs or how a fixed payload is structured depends on the folio's `contentType`. `Call_ContentTypeSpecialisation` delegates that step to the content type's own subprocess (`specialisation` in `schemas/test-data.ts`). FHIR templating (`specialisation: \"fhir-templating\"`) is one named specialisation for FHIR IG / DAK content, not the platform design."
msgstr ""

